      "description": "U+1D11E (musical G clef, surrogate pair D834+DD1E) vs U+E000 (PUA, single unit). UTF-16 sort: D834 (54324) < E000 (57344), so G clef sorts BEFORE the PUA char. Codepoint order reverses this. Rust must use UTF-16 key sort to match TS.",
      "kind": "canonicalize",
      "input_note": "Object with two keys: U+1D11E -> 1, U+E000 -> 2",
      "expected_canonical": "{\"𝄞\":1,\"\":2}",
      "ts_oracle_output": "non-bmp-canonical: {\"𝄞\":1,\"\":2}"
    },
